        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first team to reach the target score (35 or 45 game points).',
          gameplay: "Player to dealer's right leads to first trick. Each trick has four cards. Won by highest card of led suit, or highest trump if any trumps played.",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow suit if able; if void and opponent is winning the trick, must trump and beat if possible.',
            'Ten tricks per hand; winner of each trick leads to the next. Card points: 7=5, A=4, K=3, J=2, Q=1; each trick adds 1 point.',
            'Team with more than 35 card points scores the difference as game points. First team to reach agreed target (35 or 45) wins the game.',
            "Trump is determined by the dealer's bottom card (il trionfo); dealer's team scores it immediately if it is a counting card.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'The Seven (Mariglia) is the most powerful card - 5 points and unbeatable in its suit. Guard your Sevens and Aces. Remember Jacks outrank Queens.',
          intermediate: 'Create voids by discarding your only card of a suit on a trick your partner is winning. This lets you trump when that suit is led later. Track which high cards have been played.',
          advanced: "Communication strategy: The stronger partner should take control, asking specific questions while revealing minimal information. Coordinate to capture opponent's high cards. The dealer's immediate scoring from the trump indicator can be decisive - if you turn up a 7 of trumps, you score 5 points instantly.",
          tips: [
            'Track Sevens and Aces - once played, you know the highest remaining card in each suit',
            'The 10 tricks each contribute 1 bonus point - winning tricks matters even without high cards',
            "Use communication wisely - don't give opponents more information than necessary",
            "If you have multiple Sevens, you're in a very strong position",
          ],
